WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:05.771 align:start position:0% line:91%
He stars in the new movie,
"Sound of Metal,"

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:08.140 align:start position:0% line:91%
which is streaming now
on Amazon Prime Video.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.976 align:start position:0% line:85%
Here is Riz Ahmed.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:13.012 align:start position:0% line:91%
Riz, it is great to see you.
-How you doing, man?

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:15.047 align:start position:0% line:91%
Yeah, you, too.
Thanks for having me.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.815 align:start position:0% line:91%
-Thanks so much for being
on the show and coming back.

00:00:16.849 --> 00:00:19.319 line:85%
I have to say congratulations.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.488 align:start position:0% line:91%
It's some of
the best news I read.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.889 align:start position:0% line:91%
You got married
a few months ago.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.425 align:start position:0% line:91%
-I did, yeah.
I got married recently.

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:26.526 align:start position:0% line:85%
Yeah, thank you.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.094 align:start position:0% line:85%
-That's major.

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.029 size:88% position:44% line:85%
Now, look, there are stories

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:32.465 align:start position:0% line:91%
that said that
this was a secret wedding,

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:33.699 align:start position:0% line:91%
and I know you wanted
to clear this up.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:37.203 size:75% position:38% line:85%
Was it a secret wedding?

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:39.305 size:84% position:42% line:91%
-Are you saying that 'cause
I didn't invite you, Jimmy?

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:40.439 align:start position:0% line:91%
That's what's going on?
-Yes. That's exactly right.

00:00:40.472 --> 00:00:42.442 size:88% position:44% line:85%
-I sent you the invite, man.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.477 line:85%
With COVID, FedEx messed it up.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.479 align:start position:0% line:91%
I wanted you there, bro.
-Okay.

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:48.614 align:start position:0% line:91%
-You know what it is?
It's a weird one, isn't it?

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.483 align:start position:0% line:91%
I guess cause we live
in a social media age,

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:51.884 size:81% position:41% line:91%
if you don't, like, get on
the megaphone about stuff,

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.053 size:75% position:38% line:85%
it's like it's a secret.

00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:55.688 align:start position:0% line:91%
But I never know
how much is over-sharing.

00:00:55.722 --> 00:01:00.759 line:85%
Like, I'm into matcha lattes,

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:02.328 line:85%
but that's just never come up.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.764 align:start position:0% line:91%
I'm not a secret
matcha latte drinker.

00:01:04.797 --> 00:01:08.467 align:start position:0% line:91%
-[ Laughs ] Yeah, exactly, yeah.
Well, it's not a secret.

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.038 align:start position:0% line:91%
-It doesn't come up. You're
not sure what really to offer.

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:14.240 align:start position:0% line:91%
But it was kind of interesting,
you know, doing it

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:16.976 align:start position:0% line:91%
with COVID and everything
going on.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:21.347 align:start position:0% line:91%
Obviously, kept it super
intimate and socially distanced,

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.549 align:start position:0% line:91%
with just like hardly anyone
there, really.

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:26.819 align:start position:0% line:91%
Did it in a backyard,
which is nice in lots of ways.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.588 align:start position:0% line:91%
And I think
the nicest thing about it

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.791 line:85%
was you didn't have 500 aunties

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.759 align:start position:0% line:91%
hanging around you,
pinching your cheeks.

00:01:33.792 --> 00:01:36.562 line:91%
No disrespect to the aunties,
but Asian weddings are big.

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.130 size:84% position:42% line:91%
You always got these people
crawling out the woodworks

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:41.100 align:start position:0% line:91%
who I think are kind of
probably imposters.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.435 line:91%
They just smell the kebabs on
the street and just wander in.

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:45.471 align:start position:0% line:91%
Like, "Hey, I knew you
when you were a kid."

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.273 align:start position:0% line:91%
-"Do I know you?"
Yeah, exactly. Yeah.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.607 align:start position:0% line:91%
-Exactly.
-Tell me a little bit

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.109 size:88% position:44% line:85%
about your wife, if you can.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.944 align:start position:0% line:91%
How'd you meet?
-Oh, yeah, yeah. Sure, man.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.614 align:start position:0% line:91%
Yeah, well,
her name's Fatima Farheen Mirza.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.115 size:81% position:41% line:85%
She's an amazing novelist.

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:58.550 align:start position:0% line:85%
And we met so randomly

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:00.520 align:start position:0% line:91%
while actually I was preparing
for this role,

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:03.255 align:start position:0% line:91%
for "Sound of Metal,"
when I was in New York.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:07.160 size:84% position:42% line:91%
Um, we just both sat down
at the same table in a cafe

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:08.994 align:start position:0% line:91%
where we both
turned up to write.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.264 align:start position:0% line:91%
We were both, like, jostling
over the same laptop plug point.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.198 align:start position:0% line:91%
It was like a very
modern way of meeting.

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:14.466 line:85%
And we struck up a friendship,

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.303 align:start position:0% line:91%
and then we reconnected
down the line.

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:20.540 align:start position:0% line:91%
But it's weirdly like
one of the many, uh, things

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:23.109 align:start position:0% line:91%
about preparing for this role
that was so special.

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:24.877 align:start position:0% line:91%
It just brought a lot
of goodness into my life.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.146 align:start position:0% line:91%
Obviously, I met Fatima
for the first time

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.915 align:start position:0% line:91%
and met so many people
in the deaf community

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.650 size:78% position:39% line:85%
that have become friends.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:33.419 align:start position:0% line:91%
And there's just something
about this whole period

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.788 size:78% position:39% line:91%
around this film that was
kind of life-changing.

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.256 line:85%
-Yeah. Talk to me about this.

00:02:37.289 --> 00:02:39.892 align:start position:0% line:91%
"Sound of Metal" came out
a few weeks ago,

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:42.161 align:start position:0% line:91%
and you've been getting
incredible reviews.

00:02:42.194 --> 00:02:43.729 align:start position:0% line:91%
Uh, you won a Gotham Award
on Monday night.

00:02:43.762 --> 00:02:45.197 align:start position:0% line:85%
Congratulations.

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:47.066 size:75% position:38% line:85%
-Thank you, man. Thanks.

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:50.002 size:78% position:39% line:91%
-What's it like to attend
an awards show virtually?

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:51.837 align:start position:0% line:91%
-Super weird.
-It is, right?

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:55.241 line:85%
-It's weird because, you know,

00:02:55.274 --> 00:02:58.644 align:start position:0% line:91%
no one's really sure exactly
when they're on camera.

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:00.746 align:start position:0% line:91%
So you actually get
a couple of seconds

00:03:00.779 --> 00:03:04.850 align:start position:0% line:91%
of people's unadulterated,
you know, unvarnished reactions

00:03:04.883 --> 00:03:07.753 align:start position:0% line:85%
where they're like --

00:03:07.786 --> 00:03:09.688 align:start position:0% line:91%
Oh, wait, I'm on.
-Yeah, oh, I'm on, yeah.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.357 align:start position:0% line:91%
Or else they're
texting someone like,

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:12.791 align:start position:0% line:85%
"Wait, what? I'm on?"

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.927 align:start position:0% line:91%
-Yeah, so it's kind of cool
in a way,

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.663 align:start position:0% line:91%
'cause you see
a very intimate reaction.

00:03:17.696 --> 00:03:20.065 size:88% position:44% line:85%
-Dude, you crushed this one.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.934 align:start position:0% line:91%
In this movie,
you play a drummer

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:24.637 line:85%
who starts to lose his hearing.

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:28.174 align:start position:0% line:91%
And you spent months
learning to play the drums,

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:31.611 align:start position:0% line:91%
but you also learned
some sign language, as well.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:35.815 size:75% position:38% line:91%
What is it like learning
both at the same time?

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:38.618 line:91%
-It was a challenge for sure.
It was quite daunting at times.

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:42.422 align:start position:0% line:91%
I was pretty sure
I wouldn't get there.

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:45.558 align:start position:0% line:91%
Our director, Darius Marder, has
such a unique kind of vision.

00:03:45.591 --> 00:03:47.259 align:start position:0% line:91%
You won't believe
this is his first film.

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:50.263 align:start position:0% line:91%
He said he wants it all
to be as for real as possible.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.864 align:start position:0% line:91%
So when I'm playing
the drums on-screen,

00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:53.499 align:start position:0% line:91%
he wants me to be really
playing the drums.

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:56.235 align:start position:0% line:91%
When I'm signing
in American Sign Language,

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:58.204 line:85%
I'm improvising with deaf actors

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:00.773 align:start position:0% line:91%
so I have to be -- you know,
some level of fluency.

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:05.010 align:start position:0% line:91%
And so we just spent
seven months every day

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:08.114 align:start position:0% line:91%
just learning sign language,
learning the drums.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:09.114 align:start position:0% line:91%
And like I said,
it was challenging,

00:04:09.147 --> 00:04:10.749 size:88% position:44% line:85%
but I learned a lot from it.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:13.252 size:75% position:38% line:91%
And in particular, I say
that the deaf community,

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:15.554 align:start position:0% line:91%
and my sign instructor,
Jeremy Lee Stone,

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.824 align:start position:0% line:91%
who became a good friend
of mine,

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:20.392 align:start position:0% line:91%
he kind of taught me
the true meaning of listening.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.195 size:88% position:44% line:91%
You know, the deaf community
taught me the true meaning

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:25.131 align:start position:0% line:91%
of listening
and of communication.

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:27.066 align:start position:0% line:91%
It's not just something
you do with your ears.

00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:28.100 align:start position:0% line:91%
Listening is something you do
with your whole body.

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:30.002 size:75% position:38% line:85%
It's about holding space

00:04:30.035 --> 00:04:32.505 align:start position:0% line:91%
for someone else's energy
with your attention.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.206 size:81% position:41% line:91%
And in a way, I feel like
Jeremy's the best listener

00:04:34.239 --> 00:04:36.675 align:start position:0% line:91%
I've ever met. You know?
-Wow.

00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:38.510 line:91%
-So a lot of, kind of, those
lessons really stayed with me.

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:41.647 size:75% position:38% line:85%
-Did you think the drums

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.015 align:start position:0% line:91%
were, like,
"Oh, that's going to be good"?

00:04:43.049 --> 00:04:44.917 align:start position:0% line:91%
'Cause you're also a rapper
and a musician,

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:48.087 align:start position:0% line:91%
so you're like, "Oh, I can
probably keep a couple beats."

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.823 align:start position:0% line:91%
-Yeah. I actually, really
stupidly will admit,

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:52.291 size:88% position:44% line:91%
thought that the first time
I picked up the drum sticks,

00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:53.392 align:start position:0% line:91%
I'd be like, "Alright,
this will be okay."

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:54.526 size:75% position:38% line:85%
You know, I've got this.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.629 align:start position:0% line:85%
So bad.

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:59.665 align:start position:0% line:91%
Um, very different keeping time,
you know, with words

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.634 line:85%
as opposed to with your body.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.836 size:84% position:42% line:91%
The biggest challenge I had
with playing the drums was,

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:07.506 align:start position:0% line:91%
I only realized the night before
we were filming that scene,

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.675 align:start position:0% line:91%
big opening scene in the film
when I'm drumming,

00:05:09.708 --> 00:05:12.277 align:start position:0% line:91%
that I was doing this
to keep time.

00:05:15.347 --> 00:05:17.050 align:start position:0% line:91%
-What?
-Like -- Yeah.

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:18.651 align:start position:0% line:91%
I was using my jaw
as a metronome.

00:05:18.685 --> 00:05:19.918 align:start position:0% line:85%
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:22.421 align:start position:0% line:85%
-[ Humming ]

00:05:22.454 --> 00:05:23.822 align:start position:0% line:91%
-As you're playing?
-And no one thought

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.590 align:start position:0% line:91%
to tell me this
in seven months of preparation.

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:26.826 line:85%
They go, "We thought you knew.

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:28.327 align:start position:0% line:91%
We thought it was
an acting choice."

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:30.195 align:start position:0% line:85%
And I'm like, "No.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:31.530 align:start position:0% line:91%
What are you doing?"
-"Hey, you have to tell me."

00:05:31.563 --> 00:05:34.132 align:start position:0% line:91%
-So, literally,
the day we shot it,

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:37.303 line:85%
I'm using 90% of my bandwidth

00:05:37.336 --> 00:05:39.305 size:88% position:44% line:85%
just trying to keep this guy

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:42.341 size:84% position:42% line:85%
from not doing weird stuff.

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:44.243 align:start position:0% line:85%
It was weird. You know?

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:46.879 align:start position:0% line:91%
-You got enough to worry about.
You're going, "Okay."

00:05:46.912 --> 00:05:49.515 align:start position:0% line:91%
But it's also
you're playing fast, too.

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:53.285 align:start position:0% line:91%
Uh, you know, you did
something with this movie

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:56.222 line:85%
that is an interesting move --

00:05:56.255 --> 00:06:00.526 align:start position:0% line:91%
I'm sure the director thought
of this -- but the audio.

00:06:00.559 --> 00:06:02.461 align:start position:0% line:91%
Sometimes the audience
can hear everything

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:04.196 align:start position:0% line:85%
through your character.

00:06:04.229 --> 00:06:05.297 align:start position:0% line:91%
And it was --
-Yeah.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.800 align:start position:0% line:85%
-How did they do that?

00:06:07.833 --> 00:06:10.169 align:start position:0% line:91%
-Yeah. Again, our director,
Darius Marder,

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:12.104 align:start position:0% line:91%
first-time director,
but you would not believe it

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:13.773 align:start position:0% line:91%
when you see his film.
Such a bold choice.

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:15.340 line:85%
He basically wanted the audience

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:17.676 align:start position:0% line:91%
to be inside
my character's head.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.745 line:85%
So, as I'm losing my hearing,

00:06:19.778 --> 00:06:24.183 align:start position:0% line:91%
the audience starts to lose,
you know, clarity

00:06:24.216 --> 00:06:26.952 align:start position:0% line:91%
on what other characters
are saying and what's happening.

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:29.655 align:start position:0% line:91%
So it really
puts you right there

00:06:29.688 --> 00:06:31.757 align:start position:0% line:91%
and makes it quite
a physical experience.

00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:33.459 align:start position:0% line:91%
And the way they did it
was crazy.

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:36.228 size:81% position:41% line:85%
On set, after every scene,

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:40.366 align:start position:0% line:91%
the sound recordist would record
the sound of my heart,

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.834 align:start position:0% line:91%
see what my heartbeat was like
after that scene.

00:06:41.867 --> 00:06:43.636 align:start position:0% line:85%
-Wow.

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:45.003 size:78% position:39% line:85%
-Would ask me to swallow,

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:48.173 line:85%
lick my lips, blink, breathe,

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:51.410 align:start position:0% line:91%
record everything about
what's going on inside my body

00:06:51.444 --> 00:06:53.479 align:start position:0% line:91%
so that the sound design
literally puts you in my body,

00:06:53.512 --> 00:06:54.946 align:start position:0% line:85%
and you can --

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.182 line:85%
You're almost inside my head.

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:57.883 align:start position:0% line:85%
-It's amazing.

00:06:57.916 --> 00:06:59.885 align:start position:0% line:91%
For people that haven't
seen the movie,

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:02.120 align:start position:0% line:91%
can you tell everyone
what it's about?

00:07:02.154 --> 00:07:03.689 size:75% position:38% line:85%
-Yeah. I mean, in short,

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:07.259 align:start position:0% line:91%
it's the story of my character,
Ruben Stone,

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:10.897 line:91%
and his girlfriend, Lou, played
by the amazing Olivia Cooke,

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:13.332 align:start position:0% line:91%
and they live together in
this RV, in this touring band.

00:07:13.365 --> 00:07:15.667 size:84% position:42% line:85%
They're a duo in this band.

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:18.337 align:start position:0% line:91%
And all of a sudden,
Ruben loses his hearing,

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:21.507 align:start position:0% line:91%
and that threatens his band,
his relationship,

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.909 line:85%
his idea of who he thinks he is.

00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:26.912 align:start position:0% line:91%
Um, but when he starts
to kind of be accepted

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:29.682 align:start position:0% line:91%
and almost steadied
by this deaf community,

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:31.116 align:start position:0% line:91%
this community
of recovering addicts,

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.452 align:start position:0% line:91%
'cause he has a history
of addiction,

00:07:33.485 --> 00:07:36.655 align:start position:0% line:91%
he finds this kind of peace
and balance,

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:39.024 align:start position:0% line:91%
but it would mean saying goodbye
to his old life.

00:07:39.057 --> 00:07:40.993 size:84% position:42% line:85%
So he has to choose between

00:07:41.027 --> 00:07:43.028 align:start position:0% line:91%
this new kind of equilibrium
he's found

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:46.532 line:85%
or getting his old life back.

00:07:46.565 --> 00:07:47.666 line:85%
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:47.699 --> 00:07:49.768 align:start position:0% line:91%
Here's Riz Ahmed
